# Bitget keys for the crypto book — the ONLY place they live (chmod 600, never committed).
# This is the lane for an account you ALREADY have: verified Bitget, USDT-M perps, and the fee
# schedule this book is priced on (0.02 % maker / 0.06 % taker at the base tier) is what the venue
# publishes for all ten symbols — re-read it with `python3 broker_bitget.py fees`, live.
#
# Leave every line commented and the book keeps running: it scans, sizes, journals and grades on the
# SHADOW LEDGER and sends nothing. One uncommented key line is the whole arming switch.
#
# 1. Bitget app/web → Profile → API Management → Create key.
#    Permissions: **Trade only**. NOT Withdraw, NOT Transfer, NOT sub-account.
#    Set the API-key passphrase when it asks (that is the value for BITGET_API_PASSPHRASE below).
#    Bind the key to an IP range if you can — it is a second lock the venue enforces.
# 2. Paste the three values below, uncomment them, save.
# 3. launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.hermes.sentry.crypto.bitget
#    (or whichever label this folder's plist uses) — the journal prints
#    `LIVE ACK — granted by key presence`, and from the next cycle the orders are real.
#
# BITGET_API_KEY=
# BITGET_API_SECRET=
# BITGET_API_PASSPHRASE=
#
# Optional, and each one changes what the bot assumes:
# BITGET_MARGIN=isolated        # or "crossed". isolated is Bitget's own default; the bot never
#                               # raises leverage, it just uses whatever the symbol's margin mode is.
# BITGET_HEDGE=1                # only if the account is in hedge position mode. The bot otherwise
#                               # sends one-way orders (side=buy|sell, NO tradeSide) — a hedge-mode
#                               account will reject those, and the rejection is journalled, not guessed.
# BITGET_PASS_CODE=             # the fund/withdraw password some accounts require on money calls
# BITGET_SLACK=0.0015           # collar distance past a trigger for stop entries (raise it in thin books)
# BITGET_DRY=1                  # build + journal the exact payload, send NOTHING (rehearsal)
# BITGET_DRY_EQUITY=20000       # pretend-wallet size for that rehearsal
# OKX_DATA=1                    # scan OKX candles while trading Bitget (comparison run; default is
#                               default is Bitget's own history-candles, so the trigger and the tape are one venue)
#
# Before you arm this with real money, read the two lines in config.json:
#   "fees": {0.0002, 0.0006}  -> on this playbook's 0.5 % stops that is 0.24 R of every trade, and the
#                                live guard `live_max_fee_r` is 0.25 R. It passes — by 0.01 R.
#   If /fees shows your account pays more than 0.06 % taker, set "stop_floor_frac": 0.006 (wider stop,
#   target scaled with it, R unchanged) instead of raising the cap: a trade that pays the venue more
#   than it risks is a trade that loses, whatever the config says.
#
# Kill switch: comment the three key lines back out and kickstart. The next cycle falls to shadow.
# It never half-sends: a venue without a key cannot place an order, by construction.
